 ## Proof harness hygiene
 `tests/undo_coverage_proof.py` filled every required string arg with "x", so path-like args wrote a 1.2 MB LUT file `./x` into the repo root. Fixed (path-like args go to /tmp). `tests/run_proofs.sh` now fails the run when any proof leaves a stray file in the repo (checked with a stray-writing script). `tests/arc_property_proof.py` compares against an oracle binary built before the Arc flip and before central track-lock enforcement (u9l); with the stale /tmp/kimo-oracle it now fails at split_clip on a locked track (new binary errors, oracle allows). The oracle needs rebuilding from a post-u9l commit.
+
+## Render baseline, unit 8 step 0 (tests/render_bench.py, Oct 12, 640x360, release build, one core of a 2 GB box)
+Median of 5 `render_frame` calls at t=1.0 (includes MCP round trip and PNG write to /tmp), after one warm-up call.
+
+| Scene | median ms | min | max |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| background rect only | 83 | 76 | 86 |
+| + text (60 px) | 78 | 76 | 84 |
+| + ellipse with blur 20 | 92 | 85 | 102 |
+| + rect with frosted_glass | 96 | 92 | 105 |
+| + 400 dust particles | 79 | 66 | 85 |
+| + 20 translucent rects | 129 | 118 | 153 |
+
+Reading: a near-empty frame already costs about 80 ms, and every scene sits within 20 ms of it except the 20-rect scene (+46 ms, about 2.3 ms per layer). So the fixed per-call cost (frame setup, PNG encode and write, IPC) dominates these small scenes; measure that split before optimizing any single effect. Not measured: 1080p, video-source decode, multi-frame export throughput.
diff --git a/tests/render_bench.py b/tests/render_bench.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0bf6e97
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/render_bench.py
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+"""Report-only render baseline (unit 8 step 0): median wall time of render_frame per scene over 5 runs, 640x360, writes only /tmp.
+Usage: python3 tests/render_bench.py"""
+import sys, time, statistics, os; sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), '..', 'examples')); from mcp_client import Kimo
+def scene(name):
+    k = Kimo(); C = k.call; C("project_set", width=640, height=360, fps=24)
+    bg = C("add_track")["track_id"]; tr = C("add_track")["track_id"]
+    C("add_shape", track_id=bg, shape="rect", width=640, height=360, fill=[0.2, 0.3, 0.5, 1], start=0, duration=4)
+    if name == "text":
+        c = C("add_text", track_id=tr, text="Kimo render baseline", start=0, duration=4, font="Montserrat", size=60, color=[1, 1, 1], align="center")["clip_id"]
+    elif name == "blur":
+        c = C("add_shape", track_id=tr, shape="ellipse", width=300, height=200, fill=[1, 0.5, 0.2, 1], start=0, duration=4)["clip_id"]; C("add_effect", clip_id=c, kind="blur", params={"radius": 20})
+    elif name == "glass":
+        c = C("add_shape", track_id=tr, shape="rect", width=300, height=200, fill=[1, 1, 1, 1], start=0, duration=4)["clip_id"]; C("add_effect", clip_id=c, kind="frosted_glass", params={"blur": 8, "slab_thickness": 80})
+    elif name == "particles":
+        C("add_particles", track_id=tr, kind="dust", start=0, duration=4, count=400, color=[1, 0.9, 0.8], size=2, seed=7)
+    elif name == "shapes20":
+        for i in range(20): C("add_shape", track_id=tr, shape="rect", width=80, height=60, fill=[1, 1, 1, 0.5], start=0, duration=4)
+    return k
+print("scene\tmedian_ms\tmin_ms\tmax_ms")
+for n in ("empty", "text", "blur", "glass", "particles", "shapes20"):
+    k = scene(n); ts = []
+    for i in range(6):
+        a = time.perf_counter(); k.call("render_frame", time=1.0, path=f"/tmp/rb_{n}.png"); ts.append((time.perf_counter() - a) * 1000)
+    ts = ts[1:]; print(f"{n}\t{statistics.median(ts):.0f}\t{min(ts):.0f}\t{max(ts):.0f}")
